A lane file that is a dangling link: direct-domains.txt points into a folder
that does not exist (say a dotfiles link whose folder is not synced yet). The
overlay's link replaces the base fixture's file. Every command tries to seed
the lane, because nothing exists at the path, and the write cannot open
through the link. Both sides must leave the link as it is (through 3.10.1 the
shell removed it) and read the lane as empty: a read-only `list` used to end
the shell when a lane could not be read. The tree snapshot records links.
